# Internship: Full-Stack Web Developer (Angular + Express + MySQL)

**Company:** Sunflower Trip Pvt. Ltd.
**Location:** Kolkata (Hybrid; 2–3 days in office)
**Employment Type:** Paid Internship (Full-time)
**Duration:** 3–6 months
**Stipend:** ₹\[X,000] – ₹\[Y,000] / month (based on skills & availability)
**Start:** \[Immediate / From DD MMM YYYY]

## Role Overview

We’re looking for a hands-on engineering intern to help us build traveler-friendly features on domain —including **Flight API integration (Tequila by Kiwi)**, **payment gateway integration**, and enhancements to our **Angular frontend** and **Express + MySQL backend**. You’ll ship real features in JavaScript/TypeScript with guidance from our dev team.

## Key projects you’ll work on

* **Flight search (view-only):** Integrate **Tequila (Kiwi)** to power flight results; build filters (route, dates, cabin, stops), sorting, pagination, and caching.
* **Payments:** Integrate a **payment gateway** into our existing app (preferably **Razorpay**;) for deposits & bookings flow (test mode first).
* **Product features:** Angular UI components, state management, and API wiring for tours/filters; Express endpoints; MySQL queries and performance fixes.

## Responsibilities

* Build Angular components (v16+; we use v18) with clean, reusable HTML/SCSS and TypeScript.
* Create/extend Express routes for flight and payment flows; handle env configs and secrets.
* Design efficient MySQL queries (mysql2/promise), indexes, and migrations for new features.
* Implement validation, error handling, and logging (e.g., Zod/Joi, try/catch, Winston).
* Write basic unit/integration tests (Jest/Vitest or similar) where appropriate.
* Document APIs, env variables, and setup steps; create concise READMEs.
* Collaborate via Git (feature branches, PRs, code reviews).

## Must-have skills

* **JavaScript & TypeScript** (solid fundamentals).
* **Angular** (components, services, routing, forms; RxJS basics).
* **Node.js/Express** (REST APIs, middleware).
* **MySQL** (joins, aggregations, indexes; basic schema design).
* Working knowledge of Git/GitHub and Postman/Thunder Client.

## Nice-to-have

* Prior work with **Tequila (Kiwi) API** or any flight/transport API.
* **Payment gateways** (Razorpay preferred; Stripe acceptable).
* RxJS operators, Angular Material, Tailwind/SCSS.
* Basic security hygiene (env files, input validation, CORS).
* Familiarity with caching (Redis) and SSR/SEO (helpful but not required).

## Tools you’ll use

Angular 18, Express (Node 18+), MySQL, mysql2/promise, Postman, Git/GitHub, Razorpay/Stripe SDKs, Tequila API, Jira/Trello, Notion/Confluence (or similar).

## What you’ll learn

* Real-world API integrations (auth, rate limits, pagination).
* Secure payments integration & test sandbox flows.
* Performance-aware SQL and API design.
* Production-grade code reviews and release discipline.

## Eligibility

* B.Tech/BE/BCA/MCA/B.Sc (CS/IT) students or recent grads; **final-year or pre-final-year preferred**.
* Available **40 hrs/week** for the internship duration.
* Portfolio or GitHub projects to review.

